- Failure-mode changes can make a single “strength” response insufficient; conclusions must therefore be tied to fracture observations and secondary mechanical outcomes.
- Residual unexplained variation does not itself establish an unmeasured material mechanism; it may also reflect inadequate measurement resolution or model misspecification.
